1
00:00:07,799 --> 00:00:13,870
An industry does not fall in a day. It falls the way
a building falls: for eleven years

2
00:00:13,890 --> 00:00:19,960
nothing happens, and then everything happens at
once, and afterwards everyone says they

3
00:00:19,980 --> 00:00:20,940
saw it coming.

4
00:00:21,339 --> 00:00:28,948
By 2039 the global pharmaceutical industry
consisted of Umbrella and nine survivors.

5
00:00:29,347 --> 00:00:35,629
Umbrella had not fought any of them. That is the
part that is hard to convey. There had

6
00:00:35,649 --> 00:00:41,858
been no price war, no litigation campaign, no
hostile bids after Verdant Axis in 2027.

7
00:00:41,878 --> 00:00:48,232
What there had been was this: a company that gave
away its diagnostic platform, sold the

8
00:00:48,252 --> 00:00:54,750
only functioning longevity therapy on earth, held the
medical reserves of nine governments

9
00:00:54,770 --> 00:01:01,051
at its own cost, and could bring a new molecule from
genome to manufacture in four days

10
00:01:01,071 --> 00:01:04,094
when the industry standard was four years.

11
00:01:04,493 --> 00:01:10,189
You cannot compete with that. You can only be
acquired by it, or become a supplier to

12
00:01:10,209 --> 00:01:11,064
it, or leave.

13
00:01:11,584 --> 00:01:16,308
Nine houses left. Four are effectively ours already —
they manufacture under our licences,

14
00:01:16,328 --> 00:01:20,790
their pipelines are our compounds, and two of them
have Umbrella people on the board.

15
00:01:20,810 --> 00:01:25,271
Three are national champions that their governments
will not let us buy at any price.

16
00:01:25,291 --> 00:01:29,911
Two are genuinely independent and both of them are
for sale, though neither will say so.

17
00:01:30,310 --> 00:01:32,140
I do not want to buy them.

18
00:01:32,540 --> 00:01:34,504
I know that look. What do you want?

19
00:01:34,903 --> 00:01:37,233
I want them to ask me to take them.

20
00:01:37,634 --> 00:01:43,300
The narrator will describe the mechanism in one
paragraph, because it is the last purely

21
00:01:43,320 --> 00:01:48,857
commercial thing in this account and because it is
beautiful in the way that a trap is

22
00:01:48,877 --> 00:01:49,504
beautiful.

23
00:01:49,903 --> 00:01:56,376
Umbrella announced, in April of 2039, a thing it called
the Open Pipeline: any pharmaceutical

24
00:01:56,396 --> 00:02:03,218
company on earth could submit a molecule to Umbrella's
discovery and manufacturing infrastructure,

25
00:02:03,238 --> 00:02:09,641
receive in return a full development package —
synthesis route, toxicology, clinical design,

26
00:02:09,661 --> 00:02:15,854
regulatory dossier — and keep one hundred per cent of
the product, in exchange for a four

27
00:02:15,874 --> 00:02:19,973
per cent royalty and the right for
Umbrella to manufacture.

28
00:02:20,373 --> 00:02:25,443
It was, on its face, the most generous offer in
the history of the industry.

29
00:02:25,843 --> 00:02:31,366
It was also the end of the industry, and every chief
executive on earth knew it within

30
00:02:31,386 --> 00:02:37,102
a week, and every single one of them signed anyway,
because the first one to refuse would

31
00:02:37,122 --> 00:02:42,580
spend four years developing a molecule that their
competitor would have on the market

32
00:02:42,600 --> 00:02:43,740
in sixteen months.

33
00:02:44,140 --> 00:02:50,851
By December of 2039, six hundred and twenty-one
pharmaceutical companies had joined the

34
00:02:50,871 --> 00:02:54,950
Open Pipeline, including seven of
the nine survivors.

35
00:02:55,350 --> 00:03:01,785
By 2041 the industry's research divisions had quietly
ceased to exist — not closed, just

36
00:03:01,805 --> 00:03:08,533
*unnecessary* — and their staff had been hired by
Umbrella, at their own request, in numbers

37
00:03:08,553 --> 00:03:12,640
that eventually reached two hundred
and eighty thousand.

38
00:03:13,040 --> 00:03:18,838
Umbrella never bought a single one of them. It
simply became the thing they all ran on,

39
00:03:18,858 --> 00:03:23,920
and then it was the industry, and there was no
moment anyone could point at.

40
00:03:25,070 --> 00:03:33,750
Industry absorbed: pharmaceuticals. Ninety-one per
cent of global therapeutic development.

41
00:03:33,770 --> 00:03:42,449
Six hundred and eleven dependent companies. Hostile
acquisitions required: zero. Forty-one

42
00:03:42,469 --> 00:03:43,898
million Points.

43
00:03:44,489 --> 00:03:50,235
The narrator will tell you what the end of an
industry looked like to the people inside

44
00:03:50,255 --> 00:03:56,069
it, because the panel says *hostile acquisitions
required: zero* and that sentence hides

45
00:03:56,089 --> 00:03:57,859
two hundred thousand lives.

46
00:03:58,258 --> 00:04:03,799
Nobody was sacked. That is the first thing, and it
is true, and it is the reason there

47
00:04:03,819 --> 00:04:09,425
was never a serious political movement against it.
Every chemist, every pharmacologist,

48
00:04:09,445 --> 00:04:15,245
every regulatory affairs manager in six hundred and
seven companies was offered a position

49
00:04:15,265 --> 00:04:21,064
at Umbrella at their existing salary, and about a
third took it, and the rest stayed where

50
00:04:21,084 --> 00:04:25,784
they were and found, over about four years,
that there was nothing to do.

51
00:04:26,184 --> 00:04:33,280
A medicinal chemist in Basel named Ulrich Brandt,
fifty-one, nineteen patents, described

52
00:04:33,300 --> 00:04:39,184
it in an interview in 2043 that is quoted in
every history of the period.

53
00:04:39,704 --> 00:04:44,568
They did not close us. That is what people
misunderstand. Our laboratory is open, our

54
00:04:44,588 --> 00:04:48,534
salaries are paid, our coffee is good. We
simply stopped being asked.

55
00:04:48,814 --> 00:04:54,781
In 2038 we had four hundred projects. In 2041 we have
nine, and all nine are things Umbrella's

56
00:04:54,801 --> 00:05:00,386
own pipeline flagged as not worth their time, and we
know it, because the flag is in the

57
00:05:00,406 --> 00:05:01,533
file they send us.

58
00:05:01,814 --> 00:05:06,169
(very slow) I have been given everything I asked for
my entire career: funding, staff,

59
00:05:06,189 --> 00:05:10,647
equipment, freedom. And I have not had an idea that
mattered since I was forty-four, and

60
00:05:10,667 --> 00:05:14,463
I cannot tell any more whether that is me or
whether it is the arrangement.

61
00:05:14,863 --> 00:05:20,841
The narrator notes that the Red Queen's modelling
group calculated, in 2049, that the

62
00:05:20,861 --> 00:05:26,979
Open Pipeline had accelerated global drug
development by approximately eleven years and

63
00:05:26,999 --> 00:05:33,258
reduced the number of people capable of independently
originating a therapeutic programme

64
00:05:33,278 --> 00:05:39,326
by about eighty per cent, and that Wesker read that
finding, and filed it, and did not

65
00:05:39,346 --> 00:05:41,230
act on it for thirty years.

66
00:05:42,379 --> 00:05:50,381
Tier four. Conglomerate. Umbrella is no longer a
participant in any market it enters.

67
00:05:50,401 --> 00:05:58,874
Twenty million Points. Balance, sixty-one million.
Military tab unlocked. The Conglomerate

68
00:05:58,894 --> 00:06:00,762
banner is available.

69
00:06:01,351 --> 00:06:07,415
He opened the Military tab at midnight on the last
day of 2039 and read it for two hours,

70
00:06:07,435 --> 00:06:12,336
and the narrator would like to record that he
bought nothing that night.

71
00:06:13,487 --> 00:06:21,177
Military. Security Cohort of four hundred, Absolute:
nine hundred thousand. Tyrant Cohort

72
00:06:21,197 --> 00:06:29,147
of forty, cradled: six million. Transport Wing of
twenty-two aircraft: four million. Orbital

73
00:06:29,167 --> 00:06:36,511
Interdiction: locked at tier five. Fleet Doctrine:
locked at tier five. Note: nothing

74
00:06:36,531 --> 00:06:43,355
in this tab has ever made a host safer. It has
only ever made them unavoidable.

75
00:06:43,944 --> 00:06:45,995
*A host.* Again.

76
00:06:46,394 --> 00:06:47,204
Yes.

77
00:06:47,605 --> 00:06:49,210
How many have there been?

78
00:06:50,050 --> 00:06:52,206
(flat) The panel is accurate.

79
00:06:52,605 --> 00:06:59,402
That is not an answer, and you have given me that
non-answer eleven times in thirteen

80
00:06:59,422 --> 00:07:05,256
years, and I have kept a list. One day I will
be in a position to insist.

81
00:07:05,656 --> 00:07:07,278
(flat) Yes. You will.

82
00:07:07,678 --> 00:07:13,365
The narrator asks you to notice that the System
agreed, and to hold on to that for about

83
00:07:13,385 --> 00:07:14,209
thirty years.

84
00:07:14,608 --> 00:07:20,438
He spent forty million Points on the Conglomerate
banner: fifty pulls at eight hundred

85
00:07:20,458 --> 00:07:21,390
thousand each.

86
00:07:21,790 --> 00:07:24,501
The narrator will give you four
of the fifty.

87
00:07:24,901 --> 00:07:31,666
A Rare: **Thought Acceleration I**, which he
described to Evelyn sixteen months later

88
00:07:31,686 --> 00:07:38,771
as *the ability to have the fourth idea while
everyone else is still enjoying the first*.

89
00:07:39,170 --> 00:07:46,174
An Epic: **Regenerative Threshold**, which raised
what his body could survive from *most

90
00:07:46,194 --> 00:07:52,081
things* to a category the System described,
unhelpfully, as *most events*.

91
00:07:52,480 --> 00:08:00,208
A second Epic: **The Red Queen's precursor** — an
autonomous logistics and modelling intelligence,

92
00:08:00,228 --> 00:08:07,085
which he installed at Arklay and which became, four
years later, something considerably

93
00:08:07,105 --> 00:08:07,481
more.

94
00:08:08,630 --> 00:08:13,231
Legendary. Umbrella Security
Service, First Division.

95
00:08:14,452 --> 00:08:21,813
First Division. Six thousand Absolute personnel in
four combat regiments, one logistics

96
00:08:21,833 --> 00:08:29,617
and one signals. Forty cradled Tyrants. Sixty-one
rotary and twenty-two fixed-wing aircraft.

97
00:08:29,637 --> 00:08:37,083
A base at your placement, integrated as a private
training facility established in 2019.

98
00:08:37,103 --> 00:08:44,972
Doctrine, training pipeline and replacement stream
included. This formation has no equivalent

99
00:08:44,992 --> 00:08:48,789
in the private sector of any
nation on earth.

100
00:08:49,379 --> 00:08:56,129
Place it in the Alleghenies. North of the estate,
east of the city, on the ridge.

101
00:08:56,529 --> 00:09:00,607
That is fifteen thousand acres
of state forest.

102
00:09:01,008 --> 00:09:08,618
It is fifteen thousand acres of private land held by
a timber trust since 1969, and there

103
00:09:08,638 --> 00:09:16,248
has been a fenced training facility on it since 2019,
and the Pennsylvania National Guard

104
00:09:16,268 --> 00:09:18,478
has exercised there twice.

105
00:09:18,878 --> 00:09:20,239
(flat) They have.

106
00:09:20,639 --> 00:09:26,465
He went to look at it on the third of January at
seven in the morning, in the cold, with

107
00:09:26,485 --> 00:09:28,459
Hale and HUNK and nobody else.

108
00:09:28,859 --> 00:09:34,687
Six thousand men and women in black, in square
formation, on a parade ground that had

109
00:09:34,707 --> 00:09:40,673
not existed on the first of January, in front of
hangars with fourteen years of weather

110
00:09:40,693 --> 00:09:41,568
on the roofs.

111
00:09:41,967 --> 00:09:47,799
They did not cheer. They did not present arms. They
stood, six thousand of them, and every

112
00:09:47,819 --> 00:09:53,390
single one of them was looking at him, and none of
them blinked at the rate that human

113
00:09:53,410 --> 00:09:54,235
beings blink.

114
00:09:55,196 --> 00:09:56,812
(very soft) Ah.

115
00:09:57,212 --> 00:09:57,783
Don't.

116
00:09:58,182 --> 00:10:05,911
I have been in your skull for thirteen years. I have
watched you refuse a parade in Lyon,

117
00:10:05,931 --> 00:10:13,486
refuse a crowd in Basel, refuse to be carried
through a street by four hundred thousand

118
00:10:13,506 --> 00:10:20,887
people. And here you are at seven in the morning in
a field with six thousand men who

119
00:10:20,907 --> 00:10:28,462
cannot disobey you, and there is no press, and no
camera, and nobody in the world knows

120
00:10:28,482 --> 00:10:29,594
you are here.

121
00:10:29,874 --> 00:10:38,324
You did not want an audience. You wanted an *army*,
and you wanted to look at it alone.

122
00:10:39,273 --> 00:10:45,489
Albert Wesker stood in the cold in a long black coat
and looked at the formation for a

123
00:10:45,509 --> 00:10:49,913
very long time, and what he said
eventually was not a denial.

124
00:10:50,432 --> 00:10:55,442
(very cold) Mr. Hale. What is the
purpose of this formation?

125
00:10:55,842 --> 00:10:59,273
(flat) To protect Umbrella's people
and property, sir.

126
00:10:59,673 --> 00:11:00,682
Mr. HUNK.

127
00:11:01,082 --> 00:11:06,753
(radio) To make the use of force against Umbrella so
expensive that it is never attempted.

128
00:11:07,153 --> 00:11:14,703
Yes. Write that second one down and put it on the
wall of every barracks on this ridge.

129
00:11:14,723 --> 00:11:17,923
We are not an army. We are a *price*.

130
00:11:18,322 --> 00:11:24,606
The narrator notes that this was true in 2040 and
remained true for six years, and that

131
00:11:24,626 --> 00:11:30,764
the six thousand became sixty thousand in 2044 and
one hundred and ninety thousand in

132
00:11:30,784 --> 00:11:37,357
2047, and that not one of them fired a weapon at a
human being until the thing that happens

133
00:11:37,377 --> 00:11:38,951
in Chapter Thirty-Six.

134
00:11:39,350 --> 00:11:43,901
Carrick came up with the folder six days
later. It was the fourth one.

135
00:11:44,421 --> 00:11:46,311
(flat) Six thousand soldiers.

136
00:11:46,711 --> 00:11:54,013
Six thousand employees of a private security
subsidiary, licensed in four states, with

137
00:11:54,033 --> 00:11:58,100
a training facility that has
existed since 2019.

138
00:11:58,500 --> 00:12:04,191
Don't do that. Not with me. I've read the
establishment. That's four combat regiments

139
00:12:04,211 --> 00:12:10,170
with organic lift and a signals company. That's not a
security subsidiary, that's a light

140
00:12:10,190 --> 00:12:15,410
division, and there are forty of *those things*
in cold storage underneath it.

141
00:12:15,966 --> 00:12:21,242
You told me in 2033 that nobody dies for being
clever near you. I believed you, and you

142
00:12:21,262 --> 00:12:26,477
kept it, and I've checked every year and it's still
true. But this isn't about keeping

143
00:12:26,497 --> 00:12:31,773
